               </property>
               <property name="toolTip">
                 <string>A Blu-ray drive only has to supply 48 Mbit/s, and a UHD drive 109. Muxing can ask for more than that in bursts, even from a source that was itself a disc, and such an image plays from a hard disk but may stutter or refuse to start on a standalone player. This paces the disc to the limit, which is what a Blu-ray is authored to. Turn it off only if you know you want the image faster than a player can read.</string>
               </property>
               <property name="checked">
